									<div class="content">OctaneRender 2026.5.0.0 for Houdini Production (2026.5.0.0)<br>
<br>
This is a <span style="color:#FF0000">production</span> release of the <em class="text-italics">OctaneRender™ 2026.5.0.0 for Houdini™</em> plugin compiled with the <strong class="text-strong">Octane 2026.5</strong> core. This <strong class="text-strong">2026.5.0.0</strong> release is available for the latest Houdini production builds on Windows x64, Linux.<br>
<br>
<span style="color:#000080">Houdini production builds supported by this release: <strong class="text-strong">20.5.684, 21.0.700, 21.0.729, 22.0.368 and 22.0.429</strong>.</span><br>
<br>
If you are not sure if your Houdini version is compatible with the plugin - just run it and you will see an error message in case of incompatibility.<br>
<br>
<span style="font-size:120%;line-height:116%"><strong class="text-strong">Linux Note</strong></span><br>
On Linux only default Houdini builds are supported. <br>
This means that for <span style="color:#000080">Houdini 20.5, 21.0 and 22.0 <strong class="text-strong">gcc11.2</strong> builds</span> are supported.<br>
<br>
<span style="font-size:120%;line-height:116%"><strong class="text-strong">New features</strong></span><br>
To learn more about the new features and improvements of OctaneRender 2026.5, please check out the <a href="https://render.otoy.com/forum/viewtopic.php?t=85834" class="postlink">2026.5 release post</a><br>
<br>
<span style="font-size:120%;line-height:116%"><strong class="text-strong">Known bugs</strong></span><br>
On Linux, MPlay IPR may not be working. If you are having problems with it, please switch to QT5 IPR and disable "Render to MPlay" in ROP nodes.<br>
<br>
